course: dictionary
lesson: 3263
title: Equal day and night
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An equinox is one of two days each year when day and night are about the same length everywhere on Earth. The word is hard, so look at the clues around it. «At an equinox day and night are about equal» tells you the important part: equal means the same, so the two are close to the same length.
explain: Sentences also tell you when equinoxes happen. «Astronomers start the seasons at the equinoxes and solstices» shows that an equinox is a marker, like a signpost, for the start of a season. Equinoxes come in spring and in autumn, so spring and autumn are the two seasons they mark.
explain: Some clues are about what people see. «At the spring and autumn equinox a shadow snake seems to slide down the stairs» tells you the equinox is a special day that people in old Maya cities watched closely. Try your meaning in the sentence: "at the day when day and night are about equal, a shadow seems to slide down the stairs." It still makes sense, so you have it.
fact: An equinox is one of two times each year when day and night are about the same length.
fact: The two equinoxes come in spring and in autumn.
fact: Astronomers, who are scientists who study the sky, start the seasons at the equinoxes and solstices.
fact: «Spring equinox» and «autumn equinox» are the two names you will hear.
fact: The seasons are the other way round in the southern half of the world.
exercise: «At an equinox day and night are about equal.» What is an equinox? | A shadow that slides down a pyramid | A very long night in winter | A time when the sun is at its hottest | * A time when day and night are about the same length
exercise: Astronomers start spring at the equinox, about which date? | About 21 June | About 1 January | About 25 December | * About 20 March
exercise: «At the spring and autumn equinox a shadow snake seems to slide down the stairs.» Find and copy one word that names a season. | * spring | shadow | snake | stairs
test: How many equinoxes happen each year? | One | Twelve | * Two | Four
test: The story "eggs only balance on the equinox" uses the word "only". What is a good way to check it? | Count how many eggs are in the box | * Balance an egg on an ordinary day, like in May | Believe it, because a newspaper printed it | Ask whether it is a story about pyramids
exam: In the southern half of the world, how are the seasons different at the equinox? | Day is always longer than night | There are no seasons there at all | * The seasons are the other way round | The seasons are exactly the same as in the north
